1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:14,891
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is May twenty-eighth. Tokyo's Ueno Zoo just started a special event — you can visit the zoo at night, only on Saturdays. Let's listen.

2
00:00:15,492 --> 00:00:24,852
[News] 今日は楽しいニュースです。上野動物園で、新しいイベントが始まりました。

3
00:00:25,551 --> 00:00:36,975
[News] イベントの名前は「土曜の夜のどうぶつえん」です。土曜日の夜だけ、動物園に入ることができます。

4
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:47,347
[News] 時間は夜の6時から9時までです。5月と6月の土曜日、4日間あります。

5
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:56,664
[News] 一日に1000人が入ることができます。みんな、はやく予約しています。

6
00:00:57,363 --> 00:01:09,028
[News] 入園料は大人600円、子供は200円です。65歳以上のお年寄りは300円です。

7
00:01:09,727 --> 00:01:16,519
[News] 夜の動物園では、昼間と違う動物を見ることができます。

8
00:01:17,219 --> 00:01:26,147
[News] 動物園の中には美しいライトがあります。食べ物を売るお店もあります。

9
00:01:26,847 --> 00:01:39,135
[News] 上野動物園には新しい「ハシビロカート」もあります。鳥のハシビロコウのデザインの、小さい電気の車です。

10
00:01:39,835 --> 00:01:48,715
[News] 今、上野動物園にパンダはいませんが、ほかにもたくさん面白い動物がいます。

11
00:01:49,415 --> 00:01:56,927
[News] 動物園は、「子供も大人も楽しい夜になります」と話しています。

12
00:01:57,628 --> 00:01:59,260
[Host] Let's break it down.

13
00:01:59,859 --> 00:02:06,652
[Slow] 上野動物園で、新しいイベントが始まりました。

14
00:02:07,451 --> 00:02:10,044
[Host] A new event has started at Ueno Zoo.

15
00:02:10,644 --> 00:02:13,307
[Vocab] 動物園

16
00:02:13,707 --> 00:02:17,955
[Host] Zoo. The kanji literally mean animal plus garden.

17
00:02:18,556 --> 00:02:25,300
[Slow] 土曜日の夜だけ、動物園に入ることができます。

18
00:02:26,099 --> 00:02:29,003
[Host] You can enter the zoo only on Saturday nights.

19
00:02:29,604 --> 00:02:31,620
[Vocab] 夜

20
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:36,003
[Host] Night. You'll see it in today, tonight, and midnight.

21
00:02:36,604 --> 00:02:41,860
[Slow] 時間は夜の6時から9時までです。

22
00:02:42,659 --> 00:02:45,515
[Host] The hours are six to nine in the evening.

23
00:02:46,116 --> 00:02:48,443
[Vocab] 始まる

24
00:02:48,843 --> 00:02:59,500
[Host] To start, to begin. This is the form used when something starts on its own. The partner verb, with an e instead of an a, is used when a person starts something.

25
00:03:00,099 --> 00:03:05,331
[Slow] 一日に1000人が入ることができます。

26
00:03:06,132 --> 00:03:08,747
[Host] One thousand people can enter per day.

27
00:03:09,348 --> 00:03:11,747
[Vocab] 楽しい

28
00:03:12,147 --> 00:03:16,924
[Host] Fun, enjoyable. A very common everyday adjective.

29
00:03:17,524 --> 00:03:24,651
[Slow] 入園料は大人600円、子供は200円です。

30
00:03:25,451 --> 00:03:30,108
[Host] Admission is six hundred yen for adults and two hundred for children.

31
00:03:30,707 --> 00:03:32,915
[Vocab] 大人

32
00:03:33,316 --> 00:03:36,819
[Host] Adult. The kanji are big plus person.

33
00:03:37,419 --> 00:03:45,171
[Slow] 夜の動物園では、昼間と違う動物を見ることができます。

34
00:03:45,972 --> 00:03:49,475
[Host] At night, you can see animals different from daytime.

35
00:03:50,075 --> 00:03:52,187
[Vocab] 子供

36
00:03:52,587 --> 00:03:56,668
[Host] Child. Plural is the same word plus tachi.

37
00:03:57,268 --> 00:04:03,412
[Slow] 動物園の中には美しいライトがあります。

38
00:04:04,211 --> 00:04:06,900
[Host] There are beautiful lights inside the zoo.

39
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:10,092
[Vocab] 美しい

40
00:04:10,491 --> 00:04:17,307
[Host] Beautiful. A more formal word than the everyday one for pretty. Common in writing and news.

41
00:04:17,908 --> 00:04:25,012
[Slow] 鳥のハシビロコウのデザインの、小さい電気の車です。

42
00:04:25,812 --> 00:04:29,987
[Host] It is a small electric car designed after the shoebill, a bird.

43
00:04:30,588 --> 00:04:32,483
[Vocab] 鳥

44
00:04:32,884 --> 00:04:37,084
[Host] Bird. Same kanji you see in grilled chicken on a menu.

45
00:04:37,684 --> 00:04:40,684
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

46
